# The picture used in the README.

diagram "Online banking risks"

stakeholder   "The bank"                          as bank
asset         "Customer data"                     as data
asset         "Reputation"                        as rep
threat        "Script kiddie"                     as kiddie   kind=deliberate
threat        "Careless employee"                 as staff    kind=accidental
threat        "Malware"                           as malware  kind=non-human
vulnerability "Weak password policy"              as weakpw
vulnerability "Unpatched web server"              as unpatched
scenario      "Password guessed by brute force"   as guess
scenario      "Server compromised"                as compromise
incident      "Customer records leaked"           as leak
incident      "Service unavailable"               as outage
treatment     "Enforce two-factor auth"           as mfa
treatment     "Monthly patch window"              as patching
comment       "Reviewed by security team, Sept 2026" as note

bank       -> data
bank       -> rep
data       -> rep
kiddie     -> weakpw
staff      -> weakpw
malware    -> unpatched
weakpw     -> guess       "likely"
unpatched  -> compromise  "possible"
guess      -> leak        "likely"
compromise -> leak        "possible"
compromise -> outage      "rare"
leak       -> data        "major"
leak       -> rep         "moderate"
outage     -> rep         "minor"
mfa        -> guess
patching   -> unpatched
note       -> leak
